    "selection_rationale": "Evaluated 3 calibration options on out-of-fold training predictions: 'none' (Brier=0.1456, LogLoss=0.4549), 'sigmoid' (Brier=0.1457, LogLoss=0.4545), and 'isotonic' (Brier=0.1450, LogLoss=0.5422). Under the documented parsimony rule requiring \u0394Brier > 0.005 and \u0394LogLoss > 0.010 to justify post-hoc complexity, uncalibrated Logistic Regression ('none') was chosen. Logistic Regression optimizes the Bernoulli log-likelihood directly and is naturally well-calibrated via its sigmoid link; post-hoc calibration provides no meaningful gain and non-parametric isotonic regression overfits small cohorts.",
